-- title:
--   Linear preimage counts and gluing symmetric forms
-- statement:
--   Let $P_j$ denote the universally quantified source propositions represented by the finite-geometry interfaces, with all vector-space carriers in the lowest type universe. Let $B$ consist of the 26 propositions in FormGluing, and let $I$ consist of the prior Grassmann and Lagrangian propositions named below. Then
--   $$\left(\bigwedge_{j\in I}P_j\right)\Longrightarrow\bigwedge_{k\in B}P_k.$$
--   The conclusions give exact cardinalities of surjective linear preimages, probabilities for nonzero weighted form combinations, and the extension and dimension properties for gluing compatible symmetric forms across subspaces. The prior propositions are symForm_card, symmetric_nullity_probability_bound, canonicalSymplectic_nondegenerate, formGraph_isotropic, formGraph_finrank, graph_pair_intersection_finrank.
